data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** The syntax is straightforward:

```csharp
Span<nint> nints = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

It works just like any other unmanaged type with `stackalloc`. On this 64-bit system each element is 8 bytes. The only quirk is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context (since the size isn't compile-time constant), but `nint.Size` gives you the same info safely.
